# cheat — local + remote cheatsheets

## Local (your dotfiles)
  cheat                       List all local cheatsheets
  cheat <topic>               Show local cheatsheet (falls back to remote)
  cheat -e <topic>            Edit / create a local cheatsheet
  cheat -r <topic>            Force remote lookup via cheat.sh
  cheat -r <topic> <query>    Remote sub-query (e.g. cheat -r git rebase)
  cheat -s <keyword>          Search cheat.sh across all sheets
  cheat -l <lang> <query>     Language cheatsheet (e.g. cheat -l python lambda)

## Remote: Unix/Linux commands
  cheat -r tar
  cheat -r rsync
  cheat -r curl

## Remote: Language cheatsheets
  cheat -l go Pointers
  cheat -l python lambda
  cheat -l js "parse+json"        Use + for multi-word queries
  cheat -l scala Functions
  cheat -l go "reverse+a+list"    Phrase queries use + as word separator

## Remote: Multi-result paging (numbered answers)
  cheat -r python/random+string/1   First answer
  cheat -r python/random+string/2   Second answer

## Remote: Language meta-queries
  cheat -r go/:list            List all available topics for a language
  cheat -r go/:learn           Intro/primer for a language ("Learn X in Y")
  cheat -r go/:random          Random page for a language

## Remote: Search
  cheat -s snapshot            Search all sheets for keyword
  cheat -s "snapshot/r"        Recursive search across all sheets

## Remote: Special pages
  cheat -r :help               All special pages and options
  cheat -r :intro              cheat.sh introduction
  cheat -r :list               List every available cheatsheet
  cheat -r :random             Random cheatsheet

## Query options (appended to remote URLs internally)
  ?T                           Strip cheat.sh ANSI colors (bat re-colorizes)
  ?Q                           Strip text comments, code only
  ?QT                          Both — clean code, no color, no comments
